  "music": "w1-doodle-docks",
  "authorNotes": "Solo. Combines the two grabs taught in 01/02 into one crossing: the first gap (650 to 1550, 900px total) is too far for either prop alone, so it is solved by relaying — swing-combine-a (pivot 780,580) carries you out over the water, rope-combine-b (anchor 1180,520) hangs close enough to its arc's peak to grab mid-swing, and its own pendulum carries the rest of the way to the middle pier. This is the level's version of 'grab a friend': solo, the rope is standing in for a teammate's hand. On the middle pier, pose-w1-03 is the world's poseOutline — fit into the chalk silhouette and hold for the pose objective (tolerance 45), no second player required. The second gap (280px) back to the goal pier is a plain single swing (swing-final) to close the level on familiar ground. Both long gaps carry a full-span assist beam for players who'd rather skip the relay entirely."
